From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 22:32:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: expose the Xiaomi charger
 authentication interface

Add a vendor-compatible "xiaomi" sysfs group on the SM8475 layout so the
MiPPS adapter and fuel-gauge authentication daemon can run on mainline
unchanged.  Names, output formats and the request_vdm_cmd command protocol
follow qti_battery_charger.c from Xiaomi's liuqin kernel:

  request_vdm_cmd     UVDM command channel ("cmd,hexpayload")
  verify_digest       fuel-gauge HMAC challenge/response (52 byte frame)
  verify_slave_flag   selects the slave cell for verify_digest
  authentic, slave_authentic, verify_process, pd_verifed
  adapter_id, adapter_svid, pdo2, real_type, current_state,
  fastchg_mode, apdo_max, power_max, bq2597x_*

The transport gains the 52 byte digest frame next to the existing 24 byte
property and 32 byte session/authentication frames.  SET acknowledgments
are accepted either as an echo of the request frame or as the 24 byte
property reply carrying ret_code, matching the vendor driver.

Writes remain a whitelist of the properties the vendor daemon uses: the
authentication verdicts, verify_process and the UVDM command properties.
There is still no arbitrary XM property, current, voltage or PMIC write
path.  The earlier local rule that pd_verifed can only be cleared is
dropped: the userspace policy for third-party PPS adapters now lives in
the daemon, where it can be gated on cable capability.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

